{"title":"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denali compiles a list of all 5-letter strings that can be formed using the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. He lists the strings in alphabetical order starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65e7244f8a4f71e71f92226b20e4cde04eae843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AAAAA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> and ending with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfeb0fbde1a77f853e0d54345d27b197d80986c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EEEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. How many times does the letter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> occur in the 2026th string of Denali’s list?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/ecabb26c29c9b2ded0d73b08d411477ec164439d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\   1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\   2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\   3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\   4 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 5 spots where any of the 5 letters can be placed such that it produces a 5-letter string. So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1baff6050db5d3e78ff320d0358d74adf9b153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> = 3125 totals strings. And we need to figure out the 2026th string of these 3125 strings.\n</p><p>If we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5df324769ac1365d3b379a13a1f21c3333e9952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = 625 different strings, these will be the first 625 strings.\nThen if we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> we will have the 626th string all the way to the 1250th.\nThen if we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> we will have the 1251st string all the way to the 1875th.\nThen if we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> we will have the 1876th string all the way to the 2500th.\n</p><p>Since we want the 2026th string we will have our first letter to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now we repeat the same logic but for the first 2 letters:\n</p><p>If we let the first 2 letters be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = 125 different strings,  we will have the 1876th string all the way to the 2000th.\nThen if we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> we will have the 2001th string all the way to the 2125th.\n</p><p>Since we want the 2026th string we will have our first 2 letters to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>If we let the first 3 letters be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600c2c8bf2070476b38b1f452ef77d07759219f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBA$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369aa2b96d08192baf66da44577be596a58d6778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = 25 different strings,  we will have the 2001th string all the way to the 2025th.\nThen if we let the first letter be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab448881c7f4c62d685dcd110834f3522c814945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> we will have the 2026th string all the way to the 2050th.\n</p><p>Since we want the 2026th string we will have our first 3 letters to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab448881c7f4c62d685dcd110834f3522c814945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If we let the first 4 letters be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0391c7afd63556ded54330205b8450d933e18b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f9c72d91ec440826a71947c96d58c58318c97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> = 5 different strings,  we will have the 2026th string all the way to the 2030th.\n</p><p>Since we want the 2026th string we will have our first 4 letters to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0391c7afd63556ded54330205b8450d933e18b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If we let the first 5 letters be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc06eb8f66ff13620cb9736151f5e5af0d4ad613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBBAA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b9bd14ecdcc31b074b4c348e41e7be171dbde1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^0$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = 1 different strings,  we will have the 2026th string all the way to the 2026th.\n</p><p>Since we want the 2026th string we will have our first 5 letters to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc06eb8f66ff13620cb9736151f5e5af0d4ad613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBBAA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>And there it is, the 2026th string is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc06eb8f66ff13620cb9736151f5e5af0d4ad613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBBAA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, in which has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/61697162e244caa4457436f12ee92bd02bd0093c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />s.\n</p><p>~any1sgame\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034530\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 122/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5614/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37201:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034530 and revision id 287124. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}